{# One server-rendered charge row inside a purchase document's totals box — the buy-side twin of
   sales_charge_row.html.twig, and now the ONE file both PurchaseOrder and VendorBill render their
   charge rows through (they used to be two: PurchaseOrder's own macro, and VendorBill's separate
   hand-rolled `<tr>` with a different posted shape entirely — `charges[]` plus a bolted-on manual
   tax box, rather than this document's unified `charge_lines[]`. That divergence is fixed at the
   controller level too; see VendorBillController::save()).

   `type` is 'freight', 'fee' or 'tax' — the buy-side vocabulary for the sell side's
   'shipping'/'fee'/'tax' — and the row posts itself back as
   charge_lines[index][label|amount|type|slug|taxClass|placement], which
   PurchaseDocumentChargeLines turns into that line.

   No `isBuiltIn`/editable-label split the sell side's row has: a sell-side shipping row can be
   picked from a real carrier-rate lookup, so its label is protected from an accidental rename. A
   buy-side freight/fee row has no such source — every one is either typed from scratch or chosen
   off a short fixed list of common labels an admin can still correct (a vendor's invoice may not
   say "Freight" the way ours does) — so the label stays a plain editable input always, which is
   also exactly what PurchaseOrder's own charge row already did before this rewrite.

   `hook`, when passed, is 'po' (VendorBill's own JS parity is a separate pass): the remove
   control then becomes a JS-driven button (`.js-only`, hidden by CSS, removed live by app.js) with
   this real submit kept as its `.no-js-inline` fallback, exactly the pair sales_charge_row.html.twig
   renders — see that file's own note. Passed `hook: ''` (or omitted, VendorBill's current state),
   the remove control is simply this one real submit, always visible, same as before this pass
   (#full-parity, 2026-09-15).

   Parameters
   ----------
   index      required  position in the whole charge list, so the two groups (main-line vs
                        after-tax) cannot collide on the same charge_lines[i] key.
   label      required  display text.
   amount     required  the figure.
   type       required  'freight', 'fee' or 'tax'.
   slug       optional  stable reporting key that survives a relabel.
   taxClass   optional  fee rows only.
   placement  optional  fee rows only — 'main_line' | 'before_tax_line' | 'after_tax_line'.
   taxClasses required  the same {code: label} map _purchase_line_row.html.twig takes, so a fee
                        row's tax-class select shows the same labelled options a product line's
                        does — the buy-side unification of what used to be a bare-code select on
                        one document and a labelled one on the other.
   hook       optional  'po' for live JS editing, '' (default) for the original always-visible
                        real-submit-only row. #}
{% macro charge_row(index, label, amount, type, slug, taxClass, placement, taxClasses, hook) %}
    {% set placementLabels = {'main_line': 'With the goods (taxed)', 'before_tax_line': 'Before Tax', 'after_tax_line': 'After Tax'} %}
    <div class="purchase-charge-row" data-charge-type="{{ type }}">
        <span>
            {% if hook|default('') %}
                <button type="button" class="mini-action danger js-only js-{{ hook }}-remove-charge" aria-label="Remove charge">&#10005;</button>
            {% endif %}
            {# The real control: always visible when there is no JS twin (`hook` empty); the JS
               twin's no-JS fallback otherwise. Drops this row, saves and recalculates in one POST,
               the same shape as the Add Line submit on the bar below. #}
            <button type="submit" class="mini-action danger{% if hook|default('') %} no-js-inline{% endif %}" name="remove_charge_line" value="{{ index }}" aria-label="Remove charge and save">&#10005;</button>
            <input type="text" class="purchase-charge-label" name="charge_lines[{{ index }}][label]" value="{{ label }}" maxlength="120" placeholder="Enter label..." aria-label="Charge {{ index + 1 }} label">
            {% if type != 'freight' %}
                <input type="text" class="purchase-charge-slug" name="charge_lines[{{ index }}][slug]" value="{{ slug|default('') }}" maxlength="80" placeholder="slug (optional)" aria-label="Charge {{ index + 1 }} slug">
            {% endif %}
            {% if type == 'fee' %}
                <select class="purchase-charge-select" name="charge_lines[{{ index }}][taxClass]" aria-label="Charge {{ index + 1 }} tax class">
                    {% for code, taxLabel in (taxClasses|default({'E': 'Exempt', 'G': 'GST only', 'S': 'GST + PST'})) %}
                        <option value="{{ code }}"{{ (taxClass|default('E')) == code ? ' selected' : '' }}>{{ taxLabel }}</option>
                    {% endfor %}
                </select>
                {% if hook|default('') %}
                    <span class="order-charge-placement-label">{{ placementLabels[placement|default('main_line')] }}</span>
                    <input type="hidden" name="charge_lines[{{ index }}][placement]" value="{{ placement|default('main_line') }}">
                {% else %}
                    <select class="purchase-charge-select" name="charge_lines[{{ index }}][placement]" aria-label="Charge {{ index + 1 }} placement">
                        {% for value, text in placementLabels %}
                            <option value="{{ value }}"{{ (placement|default('main_line')) == value ? ' selected' : '' }}>{{ text }}</option>
                        {% endfor %}
                    </select>
                {% endif %}
            {% endif %}
        </span>
        <label>$ <input type="number" class="purchase-charge-amount{% if hook|default('') %} js-{{ hook }}-charge-amount{% endif %}" name="charge_lines[{{ index }}][amount]" min="0" step="0.01" value="{{ amount|number_format(2, '.', '') }}" aria-label="Charge {{ index + 1 }} amount"></label>
        <input type="hidden" name="charge_lines[{{ index }}][type]" value="{{ type }}">
    </div>
{% endmacro %}
